.SH NAME
.PP
auto-add-proc-mount - Configure and mount procfs under /proc

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-add-proc-mount
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
None
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-add-proc-mount
command configures procfs in /etc/fstab and immediately mounts it
at /proc.

Note that procfs is deprecated on FreeBSD, where process information
is (more efficiently) retrieved directly using libprocstat(3)
and kvm(3) system calls, or via the procstat(1) command,
rather than by opening, parsing, and closing files under /proc.

Nevertheless, /proc may be required by some programs ported
from other Unix-compatible systems.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-add-proc-mount
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/proc, /etc/fstab
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), procfs(4), procstat(1), libprocstat(3), kvm(3)

